#. Context: Help › explanation of the Graham Number. Use the local decimal
#. separator in 22.5.
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:59
msgid ""
"√(22.5 × EPS × book value per share) — Benjamin Graham's classic value formula. Needs "
"positive trailing earnings and book value per share."
msgstr ""
"√(22.5 × EPS × book value per share) — Benjamin Graham's classic value formula. Needs "
"positive trailing earnings and book value per share."

#. Context: Help › valuation model name: fair value from a fair P/E multiple
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:61
msgid "PE Fair Value"
msgstr "PE Fair Value"

#. Context: Help › explanation of the P/E fair value model
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:61
msgid "Trailing EPS × a sector-typical fair P/E multiple."
msgstr "Trailing EPS × a sector-typical fair P/E multiple."

#. Context: Help › valuation model name (kept in English)
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:62
msgid "EPV (Earnings Power Value)"
msgstr "EPV (Earnings Power Value)"

#. Context: Help › explanation of EPV
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:62
msgid ""
"Normalised earnings capitalised at the cost of capital, deliberately ignoring "
"speculative growth."
msgstr ""
"Normalised earnings capitalised at the cost of capital, deliberately ignoring "
"speculative growth."

#. Context: Help › valuation model name: one-stage dividend discount model
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:64
msgid "DDM — 1-stage"
msgstr "DDM — 1-stage"

#. Context: Help › explanation of the one-stage DDM
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:64
msgid ""
"Gordon growth model: next year's expected dividend discounted at (cost of equity − "
"perpetual growth rate). Only applies to dividend payers."
msgstr ""
"Gordon growth model: next year's expected dividend discounted at (cost of equity − "
"perpetual growth rate). Only applies to dividend payers."

#. Context: Help › valuation model name: two-stage dividend discount model
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:66
msgid "DDM — 2-stage"
msgstr "DDM — 2-stage"

#. Context: Help › explanation of the two-stage DDM
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:66
msgid ""
"A higher-growth phase followed by a stable terminal-growth phase, each discounted back "
"separately. Also dividend-payer only."
msgstr ""
"A higher-growth phase followed by a stable terminal-growth phase, each discounted back "
"separately. Also dividend-payer only."

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:68
msgid "Book value and FCF fallbacks"
msgstr "Book value and FCF fallbacks"

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:68
msgid ""
"Used only when Graham, P/E and EPV all fail (typically a loss-maker): book value"
" × a sector P/B multiple, and free cash flow × a fixed multiple."
msgstr ""
"Used only when Graham, P/E and EPV all fail (typically a loss-maker): "
"book value × a sector P/B multiple, and free cash flow × a fixed "
"multiple."

#. Context: Help › FAQ question
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:76
msgid "How is the composite fair value calculated?"
msgstr "How is the composite fair value calculated?"

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:77
msgid ""
"Each stock is valued by every model that applies to it. Their values are "
"combined into one weighted fair value, capped when a single model runs far above"
" the others. Margin of safety is the discount of the price to that figure. Both "
"are model estimates."
msgstr ""
"Each stock is valued by every model that applies to it. Their values are "
"combined into one weighted fair value, capped when a single model runs "
"far above the others. Margin of safety is the discount of the price to "
"that figure. Both are model estimates."

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:80
msgid "What does the weighted composite score mean?"
msgstr "What does the weighted composite score mean?"

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:81
msgid ""
"A 0–100 value-weighted mean of the model scores across your holdings. It "
"describes the portfolio; it is not a recommendation. A holding that fails a "
"quality screen counts with its score of 0; a holding without a score (No signal)"
" is left out."
msgstr ""
"A 0–100 value-weighted mean of the model scores across your holdings. It "
"describes the portfolio; it is not a recommendation. A holding that fails"
" a quality screen counts with its score of 0; a holding without a score "
"(No signal) is left out."

#. Context: Help › FAQ question
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:84
msgid "How often do prices update?"
msgstr "How often do prices update?"

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:85
msgid ""
"During the beta, prices are delayed quotes from Yahoo Finance that refresh on "
"the interval set in Settings → Data during market hours. Fundamentals refresh "
"about every 24 hours, and the signals are recomputed when they do. Every signal "
"shows the time of its price."
msgstr ""
"During the beta, prices are delayed quotes from Yahoo Finance that "
"refresh on the interval set in Settings → Data during market hours. "
"Fundamentals refresh about every 24 hours, and the signals are recomputed"
" when they do. Every signal shows the time of its price."

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:88
msgid "Why does a stock show “Fails quality screen”?"
msgstr "Why does a stock show “Fails quality screen”?"

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:89
msgid ""
"It breaks one of the quality rules listed on this page; the explanation next to "
"the badge names which. Its composite score is set to 0. It still appears in your"
" portfolio and valuations."
msgstr ""
"It breaks one of the quality rules listed on this page; the explanation "
"next to the badge names which. Its composite score is set to 0. It still "
"appears in your portfolio and valuations."

